<article class="env-remarks" id="02F5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02F5">Remarks <span data-tag="02F5">111.49.2</span>.</a> Here are some trivial remarks. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
On a Noetherian integral scheme $X$ the sheaf ${\mathcal K}_ X$ is constant with value the function field $K(X)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
To make sense out of the definitions above one needs to show that 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \text{length}_{\mathcal O}({\mathcal O}/(ab)) = \text{length}_{\mathcal O}({\mathcal O}/(a)) + \text{length}_{\mathcal O}({\mathcal O}/(b))  \]
</div>
<p>
 for any pair $(a, b)$ of nonzero elements of a Noetherian 1-dimensional local domain ${\mathcal O}$. This will be done in the lectures. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>